    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d140">

                <pb facs="0283" n="171" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg171"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20261/16: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate Peace to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-02-11T19:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 11,
                                1919, 7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 12, 12:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>688. Department’s telegram 563, February 4, 5 p.m.<anchor n="40" xml:id="d140-f1"
                    /></p>
                <p>Please see telegram of February 10th, 1569, from the Minister at Christiania
                    proposing the release of Kalamatiano and English mission against the Soviet
                    authorities arrested at Blagovestchensk. Suggest we cannot consider proposal
                    unless it includes Tredwell. Please advise action taken.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
